{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_schema_registry_inmemoryschemaregistry", "label": "InMemorySchemaRegistry", "file_type": "document", "rationale": "The optional catalog for larger codebases: register each (manifest, version) once with the codec that validates it and the upcaster that brings the previous version forward, and the registry builds the adapters. register mutates in place and re-registering a pair overwrites it. Reach for it at 10+ event types.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/migration/schema-registry.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_schema_registry_schemaregistry", "label": "SchemaRegistry interface", "file_type": "document", "rationale": "register / get / latestVersion / list / eventAdapter / snapshotAdapter. It is an interface so a different backing store can be implemented; InMemorySchemaRegistry is the shipped one and keeps all state in one process.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/migration/schema-registry.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_schema_registry_schemaregistration", "label": "SchemaRegistration", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/migration/schema-registry.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_schema_registry_zodcodec", "label": "zodCodec", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/migration/schema-registry.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_schema_registry_serializercodec", "label": "serializerCodec", "file_type": "document", "rationale": "Wraps any Serializer (Avro, Protobuf) so each version can use a different wire format. It encodes to { serializerId, manifest, bytes } and stops there \u2014 the journal's own payload codec already carries a Uint8Array as tagged JSON, so the bytes are base64'd exactly once. The serializerId travels with the row, which makes a format mismatch loud instead of decoding into nonsense.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/migration/schema-registry.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_schema_registry_compatibility_checks", "label": "Register-time compatibility checks", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "'none' skips the check, 'backward' requires the previous version plus an upcastFromPrev, and 'sample' additionally round-trips a supplied sample (decode with the previous codec, upcast, re-encode with the new one). Bump a version but forget the upcaster and registration fails loud at startup instead of at first replay.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/migration/schema-registry.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_schema_registry_per_version_wire_format", "label": "A binary wire format per version", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The codec layer is the only place a per-version format switch works, because a store's withSerializer(...) is store-wide \u2014 one format for every payload it writes. Avro rows already on disk keep decoding through the v1 codec while new events are written as Protobuf; both formats coexist in one stream.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/migration/schema-registry.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_schema_registry_not_a_remote_schema_registry", "label": "Not a remote schema registry", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "No remote subject-versioning or over-the-wire compatibility negotiation \u2014 out of scope for v1. The structural schema is still here: every (manifest, version) carries a codec enforced on read and write. Treat the registry as per-deployment, a constant in code rather than differing runtime state per environment.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/migration/schema-registry.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_schema_registry_inmemoryschemaregistry", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_schema_registry_schemaregistry", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/migration/schema-registry.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_schema_registry_compatibility_checks", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_schema_registry_inmemoryschemaregistry", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/migration/schema-registry.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_schema_registry_per_version_wire_format", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_schema_registry_serializercodec", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/migration/schema-registry.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_schema_registry_not_a_remote_schema_registry", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_schema_registry_schemaregistry", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/migration/schema-registry.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_schema_registry_inmemoryschemaregistry", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_migrating_adapter_migratingadapter", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/migration/schema-registry.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_schema_registry_schemaregistration", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_schema_registry_zodcodec", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/migration/schema-registry.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_schema_registry_compatibility_checks", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_migrating_adapter_chain_gap_migrationerror", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/migration/schema-registry.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": []}